Subject: [PATCH 1/3] readline: an idle-reader mailbox, reader events and a pre-EOF decision

Readline returns pending and macro input without consulting the character callback, and
rl_gather_tyi can call that callback while it fills a buffer, before preceding characters have
changed rl_end. So a private mailbox is read at the one point where the reader has taken everything
it had buffered and is waiting for the terminal, and the reader also waits on that mailbox
alongside the terminal. The reader answers it in place: it publishes what its own queues hold,
installs and accepts a line, and ends a pending key wait by returning a negative key, which every
existing caller already turns into its own abort with the edit buffer intact.

The end-of-file decision is taken immediately before Readline's own end-of-file branch, after the
next character has been selected from its input sources. It answers native or consume and replaces
no binding, so a shell's ignoreeof setting is left exactly as it is.

